{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I am HaShem your Elohim.</b> Rabbi Levi said: the Holy One, blessed be He, appeared to Israel like an icon that has a face in every direction — a thousand people gaze at it and it gazes at all of them. So too the Holy One, blessed be He: when He spoke, each and every one of Israel said, 'He is speaking with me.' For it is not written אנכי ה׳ אלהיכם, but rather אלהיך — because He spoke with each and every one according to the order in which they stood around the mountain, as it is written: 'and you shall bound the people round about, saying.' And do not wonder at this, for the manna — each one tasted it according to his strength; if the manna was so, how much more so the divine speech." "<b>HaShem your Elohim.</b> I have already explained this in the portion of Bereshit." "<b>I am HaShem your Elohim.</b> This is the first utterance. 'I' — I command you to hold Me as your master, because I brought you out of the land of Egypt, and I have a claim of lordship over you. <b>From the house of slaves.</b> And it is better for you to serve Me than to serve them as slaves." "<b>Who brought you out.</b> He could have said 'who made you' or 'who created you,' and likewise many kindnesses that He does for His creatures, to say that the Holy One, blessed be He, has a claim upon us to accept His commandments. But had He said so, they could have replied: did You not do likewise for all the other nations, so why do You impose upon us for this the yoke of Your Torah? Therefore He set before them what He did not do for any other nation or people."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:57.784711541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}